#
# The problem reporter at boot: whether the boot before this one ended in a shutdown at all, then a
# first look for problems (scripts/xgs/reporter.py boot). Detached, so the boot never waits for it,
# and so a relay that cannot be reached yet - the WAN may still be coming up - costs nothing: the
# plugin's five-minute cron entry sends what is waiting.
#
# First, the reset's cause that 06-xgs-reset-reason kept is moved to this boot's time as it reads now
# (scripts/xgs/reset_reason.py follow): the reporter tells this boot's record by that time, within
# five seconds, and ntpd's first step can come between the two hooks. Until 2026-11-06 a step of more
# than five seconds there left the cause out of the report of a restart without a shutdown.

RR=/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/xgs/reset_reason.py
[ -x "${RR}" ] && "${RR}" follow > /dev/null 2>&1
R=/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/xgs/reporter.py
[ -x "${R}" ] || exit 0
/usr/sbin/daemon -f "${R}" boot
exit 0
